<title>COMOROS: Striking civil servants demonstrate in Comoros.</title>
<headline>Striking civil servants demonstrate in Comoros.</headline>
<dateline>MORONI 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking civil servants in the Comoro Islands set up roadblocks and burned tyres on Wednesday, bringing traffic in the capital to a halt in their campaign to be paid.</p>
<p>The civil servants on the Indian Ocean islands archipelago are owed up to 12 months of pay. The protest was designed to prevent heavily guarded employees of the Office of the Paymaster reaching their offices to pay salaries for January.</p>
<p>Trade unionists say they fear the arrears will be frozen if the January salaries are paid.</p>
<p>Police and soldiers dismantled the roadblocks and extinguished the tyres set up by groups of the strikers.</p>
</text>
